    "Текст записи:<div class=\"eng-text\"><p>Text A. Dear guests, welcome to the bear area in our zoo. The good news is that a week ago, a new baby bear was born. His mom had arrived from a Canadian zoo, and after the due quarantine, joined our family of bears. The quarantine is a necessary procedure in such cases. The baby bear, whose name is Willie, is very cute. Unfortunately, the baby is out of sight now. He's in the cave with his mom, fast asleep. Like all babies, Willie sleeps most of the day. Text B. Hi, Vicki, it's Paul. I'm calling to tell you about our schedule for tomorrow. There are a few changes while you're away. First of all, the math test is canceled. Instead of that, we're going to have science. Miss Adams reminded us that tomorrow we need to be ready with our presentations on chemical elements. In science class, she's going to see all of them. As for the essay about outstanding people, forget about it for a while. It's been put off till next week. See you. Text C. Hi, Maya. You look great. Hi, Jeff. Probably because it's my birthday today. I've turned 15. Many happy returns. Are you having a party tonight? No, we've decided to throw it sometime later. My exam session started two days ago, so I'm really busy now. No time for partying. In a fortnight, when the holidays start, I'll invite all my friends to the party. Will you come? Yes, if it's not at the weekend. I've already got plans for the weekends till the end of the month. No, no, it's going to be a Thursday. Not next Thursday, but the Thursday after. Okay, I understand. Text D. What are you doing this summer, Jess? We haven't got any definite plans yet, Harry. We may go to my aunt's house. She lives in France. Sounds great. I love it too. But mum insists on going to Berlin. She wants me to practice German. I don't like the idea, and my German is okay anyway. Don't you like Germany? I definitely prefer the French countryside to Germany or Britain. And I've got cousins there. We usually have so much fun together. And you can practice your French there, can't you? Not really. My cousins are learning English and want me to speak English, so they can practice.</p></div>"
