    "Текст записи:<div class=\"eng-text\"><p>Text A. And finally, I would like to tell you about your exam on Monday. It's going to be a computer-based exam. You'll be using the computers in our computer room, so do not bring your own ones. You'll have to leave them on the reception desk anyway. You can keep your mobile phones on you, but remember that you mustn't use them for any purpose. If you do, your test will not be graded. No textbooks or notebooks, of course. All you should bring is your student card, a pen, and a bottle of water. Text B. Hi, Dad. I've already arrived but can see neither you nor Mom. There are so many people at the arrivals, it's easy to lose each other. So I'm waiting for you at the staircase, which is in the arrival lounge, to the right of the entrance to the terminal. I'm wearing a brand new blue coat bought from a Parisian shopping center. I'm awfully hungry and suggest going to our favorite cafe straight from the airport. That one in the city center where we celebrated my birthday. See you. Text C. Look, there are so many people in the square. It's just a book fair, but it's the first time we've had an event like this in our town. Except for the Folk Music Festival last May. Oh, it was wonderful, remember? People were singing and dancing for two days. Do you know anything about this fair? I've heard it displays fiction, art books, business literature, and books for children. A few writers will be introducing their books. Ron Smith, an athlete, is going to present his book on the marathons he's taken part in. Why not see it? Where can we buy the entrance tickets? No need. It's free. Text D. Leo, can I ask you a favor? Sure, Anne. What's that? I've got a pen friend from Germany. We communicate in English, but I want to send her a handmade birthday card in German. Wow, I don't remember the last time I received a paper card. Probably never. And what do you want me to do? Print the card? No, my German is not good enough for writing birthday wishes. Could you help me with it? Okay, let's meet up in the design room after classes. It'll take a few minutes to write the wishes. Thanks. Are you planning to send her just a card or a present too? A special souvenir. I bought it long ago.</p></div>"
